<task id="173" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Child records show their parent's Access Permission: To Do, Event, Communication and Document carry the parent's sprk_accesspermission, written once in the shared stamp path and kept in step by the secure-child reconcile; a parentless child keeps its own value (owner round 81)</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — UAC defect remediation (owner round 81, 2026-10-08)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the shared child write path (CoreAncestorResolver / RecordOwnershipResolver callers) and the SecureChildReconciliationJob, adds a form library and a schema script, and modifies tests (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Owner-requested tier. Cross-cutting: every child create path of four tables, the 2-minute reconcile and live forms; it reverses part of task 138's retirement, so stale rules elsewhere must be found and corrected.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits SecureChildReconciliationJob / SecureChildReconciler (issue #1378 touches the same pass) and rewrites live form XML on sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication and sprk_document; no other formxml writer may run against dev at the same time (task 168 rule).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, forms, webresource, job, testing, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>UAT 2026-10-08: a To Do created through the Word web add-in on a document under Restricted matter PAT-176903 showed Access Permission = Standard. Peer trace (spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1): ownership was correct, but no BFF path writes sprk_todo.sprk_accesspermission. Owner round 81 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md) decides the behaviour; round 82 is the related "parent permissions control" rule.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make sprk_accesspermission on To Do, Event, Communication and Document show the value inherited from the record's parents whenever it has a parent, and leave a parentless record's own user-set value alone. Compute and write the value server-side in the ONE shared child stamp path, keep it in step through SecureChildReconciliationJob, lock the field on the forms while a parent exists, bring sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission into source, and correct every doc and comment that still calls the child column retired.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: .NET 10 BFF (Dataverse write path, IScheduledJob reconcile), Dataverse form XML and form web resources, PowerShell operator scripts over the Web API.</role>

  <goal>After this task:
(1) EFFECTIVE VALUE RULE. For a row of sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication or sprk_document: walk its parent lookups (the table's lineage in SecureChildLineage, the single source of which lookups count) up to records that have no parent (a root sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_workassignment, or a parentless child). The inherited value is the MOST RESTRICTIVE own sprk_accesspermission among those top records: Restricted (100000002) over Limited (100000001) over Standard (100000000); a null counts as Standard. A row with no non-null parent lookup has no inherited value: its own value is user-set and never overwritten.
(2) CREATE AND RE-FILE. Every server create or re-file of these four tables that already goes through CoreAncestorResolver.StampAsync / DeriveForHostAsync writes the inherited value in the same payload. It is implemented ONCE in a shared helper called from that path, never in Office-only or endpoint-local code. A failed read leaves the column untouched (no Standard written by default) and is logged; it does not fail the create, since the value is display-only.
(3) RECONCILE. SecureChildReconciliationJob's recent-changes pass corrects drift within its normal cycle: a child re-filed by a client or the Web API, a child whose parent's value changed (descending from changed roots and changed parentless children through the existing scoped downward walk), and a hand edit of a parented child's value. Writes go only to rows whose stored value differs.
(4) NO ENFORCEMENT CHANGE. No access decision reads a child table's sprk_accesspermission. Enforcement keeps reading the root flags (ExternalParticipationService.GetRootRecordFlagsAsync and the secure-root path). A parentless child's value is recorded only (owner, round 81: "This is fine (BUT in future we might need to revisit)").
(5) FORMS. On every Main and Quick Create form of the four tables that shows sprk_accesspermission, the control is read-only while any filing column in config/regarding-filing-columns.json (task 168's list) is non-null, with an info-level form notification "Access permission is inherited from {parent name}". It is editable when there is no parent. No TrackingFieldTrio is added to sprk_communication (owner). Applied by a checked-in, idempotent operator script with dry run, -Apply (snapshot first), -Verify and -RestoreFrom, modelled on scripts/Add-RegardingFilingPickerToForms.ps1.
(6) SCHEMA IN SOURCE. sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission (added live by the owner 2026-10-08) is bound to the same global choice as the roots, is in the SpaarkeCore solution (Test-DvInSolution from scripts/common/DataverseSolutionMembership.ps1), and is documented in docs/data-model.
(7) DOCS. docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md (the "retired column" section, line 12 onward), projects/unified-access-control-r2/unified-access-control-cascade.md:37, docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md:527, the remarks in ExternalParticipationService.cs (~line 871), EmailWorkspace.mapping.ts:42 and TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts:119 describe the column as a display copy of the parent's value that enforcement never reads. scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 is deleted, because running it would destroy a column the owner now uses. Record the supersession in notes/decisions.md.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Round 81 (and the peer's advice, current-task.md "Round 81"): show the parent's value, write it once in the shared stamp path, keep it in step by the reconcile. Round 2 Q6 / task 138 had retired sprk_communication.sprk_accesspermission; round 81 extends that rule: the column returns as an inherited DISPLAY copy and enforcement still reads the root. Round 82: the parent's permissions control a filed child.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs (StampAsync at ~726/750, DeriveForHostAsync)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs (per-table parent lookups)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildReconciliationJob.cs, SecureChildReconciler.cs, SecureChildShareSynchronizer.cs (already reads the root's sprk_accesspermission at ~1019)</file>
      <file>Create paths to enumerate (grep StampAsync / DeriveForHostAsync callers): Services/Office/OfficeService.cs (CreateTodoAsync ~2067), Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs, Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs, Api/DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs, Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs, the wizard and AI to-do writers</file>
      <file>config/regarding-filing-columns.json; scripts/Add-RegardingFilingPickerToForms.ps1 (form-script reference); scripts/common/DataverseSolutionMembership.ps1</file>
      <file>Docs listed in goal (7); scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 (delete)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §17 / ADR-002">No Dataverse plugin. One server-side owner for the invariant: a single shared helper, called from the stamp path and the reconcile. No client writes the inherited value (the form only locks and labels).</constraint>
    <constraint source="round 81">Never overwrite the own value of a row with no non-null parent lookup, including on re-file to "no parent": the last value stays and becomes editable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="round 2 Q6 / round 81">No code added or changed in this task may read sprk_accesspermission from sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication or sprk_document for an access decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036 / ADR-052">Extend SecureChildReconciliationJob; do not add a new job or timer. Keep its one-try-per-table behaviour (#1378 is filed separately; do not widen it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: placement statement, publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE. No new endpoint.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Any new file (helper, form web resource, script) carries the three-question justification in the task notes; prefer extending an existing per-table form library over a new one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 168">Form XML writes are whole-document rewrites: snapshot before write; never run while another formxml script runs against dev.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md">Agents make no app-setting, Entra or Key Vault changes. Live -Apply runs (schema, forms, web resource) are main-session gates unless the main session delegates them.</constraint>
  </constraints>

