    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read round 81/82. Live, read-only: confirm sprk_accesspermission exists on all four tables, is bound to the roots' global choice, and which forms show it.</step>
    <step order="2">Enumerate every create/re-file path of the four tables (server StampAsync/DeriveForHostAsync callers, and client or Web API paths that bypass them); list them in the notes with which mechanism covers each (stamp path or reconcile).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the shared inherited-value helper over SecureChildLineage; wire it into the stamp path; unit tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend SecureChildReconciliationJob for drift (re-file, parent change, hand edit); tests including the downward walk.</step>
    <step order="5">Form library + form-lock script (dry run / -Apply / -Verify / -RestoreFrom / -SelfTest) and the sprk_document schema/solution script with -Verify.</step>
    <step order="6">Docs and comments (goal 7); delete the retire script; record the supersession.</step>
    <step order="7">Full test suites, publish delta, open the PR. Update TASK-INDEX (🔄 [wip] → ✅ [done] only after the live gate) and the POML status; run scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If sprk_accesspermission on any of the four tables is NOT bound to the roots' global choice, or carries different option values, STOP and escalate before writing anything.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an existing access decision already reads a child table's sprk_accesspermission (check SpeContainerMembershipSync.cs ~420 and OfficeEditAccessService.cs ~235 for which tables reach them), STOP and report: writing the inherited value would change enforcement.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a create path for these tables writes stamps without CoreAncestorResolver and the reconcile cannot see the row within its cycle, report it as a first-class stop with the proposed fix.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Shared helper (location chosen by the executor, next to CoreAncestorResolver) + its wiring</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildReconciliationJob.cs (and reconciler) changes</output>
    <output type="code">Form library and scripts/ form-lock script; scripts/ schema script for sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission</output>
    <output type="test">Unit/integration tests beside the existing CoreAncestorResolver and SecureChildReconciliationJob tests; script -SelfTest fixtures</output>
    <output type="docs">Goal (7) files; projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-173-child-access-permission.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A To Do created through POST /api/office/todo on a document under a Restricted matter is created with sprk_accesspermission = Restricted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A child with two roots, Standard and Limited, gets Limited; with Limited and Restricted, Restricted; with all parents null-valued, Standard.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A To Do on a parentless Document whose own value is Restricted gets Restricted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A parentless child created with Limited keeps Limited after create and after every reconcile run; un-filing a child keeps its last value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unreadable parent or a lineage past MaxLineageDepth leaves the stored value unchanged, logs a warning, and does not fail the create.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing a matter from Standard to Restricted updates its existing To Do, Event, Communication and Document children within one reconcile cycle; a hand edit of a parented child to Standard is reverted in one cycle; rows already correct are not written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No changed or added code reads a child table's sprk_accesspermission for an access decision (shown by grep in the notes); existing enforcement tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On the forms, the field is read-only with the "inherited from" notification when a filing column is set, editable when none is set; -Verify passes after -Apply and fails on a re-opened control.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_document.sprk_accesspermission is in SpaarkeCore, bound to the roots' global choice, and -Verify passes; scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 no longer exists and no doc references it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the rule in goal (1), the create and reconcile paths, and the negative cases named above. Request one seeding proof only for "a parentless own value is never overwritten". Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All BFF unit, integration and ArchTests suites pass; publish delta is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">LIVE GATE (dev, after deploy): repeat the owner's UAT — a To Do created through the Word web add-in on a document under PAT-176903 shows Restricted, with the field locked and labelled on the To Do form.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Inherited and locked on a parented To Do">
      <url>https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_todo</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open a To Do filed under a Restricted matter</step>
        <step>Verify Access Permission shows Restricted, is read-only, and the info notification names the parent</step>
        <step>Check the console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Locked, labelled, no console errors; the same holds for an Event, a Communication and a Document</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Editable on a parentless record">
      <steps>
        <step>Create a To Do with no regarding record; set Access Permission to Limited; save; reopen</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The field is editable and keeps Limited after the next reconcile cycle</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files, follow task-execute, and record decisions and the create-path inventory in notes/task-173-child-access-permission.md.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
